    "text": {
     "en": "The Vedas are the oldest texts of India, composed in Sanskrit and passed on by memory for many years. There are four: Rigveda, Samaveda, Yajurveda and Atharvaveda.\nVedic society valued learning, farming, cattle rearing and nature. People worshipped natural forces and performed yajnas.\nThe Vedas also led to later thought such as the Upanishads."
    }
